        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Trilochanpala, Anandapala\n- Organizations: Kabul Shahis, Shahiya\n- Places: Kabul Valley, Gandhara, eastern Afghanistan, northern Pakistan\n- Concepts: Classical Period of India, Kushan Empire decline\n- Roles: king\n\nFacts:\n- The Kabul Shahi dynasties, also called Shahiya, ruled the Kabul Valley in eastern Afghanistan and the old province of Gandhara in northern Pakistan from the decline of the Kushan Empire in the 3rd century until the early 11th century during the Classical Period of India.\n- Trilochanpala was the son of Anandapala.\n- Trilochanpala was the last king of the Kabul Shahis.",
